# path

Path text: joining and splitting file paths.

**Pure** — importable by default.

A module page lists its functions alphabetically, whatever their source order, then its constants, alphabetically
too: [`path_separator`](#path_separator) joins the parts.

## Functions

- [`base(p) -> string`](#base)
- [`join(...parts) -> string`](#join)

<a id="base"></a>
### `base(p) -> string`

Answer the last element.

<a id="join"></a>
### `join(...parts) -> string`

Join the parts with the separator.

```go
path.join("a", "b")   // "a/b"
```

## Constants

- [`path_list_separator -> rune`](#path_list_separator)
- [`path_separator -> rune`](#path_separator)

<a id="path_list_separator"></a>
### `path_list_separator -> rune`

The separator of the paths in a list.

<a id="path_separator"></a>
### `path_separator -> rune`

The separator of path elements, written by [`join`](#join).

The list separator is [`path_list_separator`](#path_list_separator).

```go
path.path_separator   // => '/'
```
